urname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Coffey</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pyrrolidinedithiocarbamate increases the therapeutic index of 5-fluorouracil in a mouse model</article-title><source>Gastroenterology</source><year>2000</year><volume>118</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>89</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Gastroenterology||118|81||bib4|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10611156</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bach</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Williamson</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Marshman</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Dwyer</surname><given-names>ST</given-names></name><name><surname>Potten</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The antioxidant <italic>n</italic>-acetylcysteine increases 5-fluorouracil activity against colorectal cancer xenografts in nude mice</article-title><source>J Gastrointest Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Gastrointest Surg||5|91||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11309653</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruck</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Aeed</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Schey</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Matas</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Reifen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Zaiger</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Hochman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Avni</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pyrrolidine dithiocarbamate protects against thioacetamide-induced fulminant hepatic failure in rats</article-title><source>J Hepatol</source><year>2002</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>370</fpage><lpage>377</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Hepatol||36|370||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11867181</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bunz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Hwang</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Torrance</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Waldman</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Dillehay</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lengauer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kinzler</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name><name><surname>Vogelstein</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Disruption of p53 in human cancer cells alters the responses to therapeutic agents [see comments]</article-title><source>J Clin Invest</source><year>1999</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>269</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Invest||104|263||bib7|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10430607</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burns</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Beland</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of biological time on the determination of the LD<sub>50</sub> of 5-fluorouracil in mice</article-title><source>Pharmacology</source><year>1984</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>296</fpage><lpage>300</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Pharmacology||28|296||bib8|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6728904</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buroker</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Connell</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wieand</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Krook</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerstner</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Mailliard</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schaefer</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Levitt</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Kardinal</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Gesme</surname><given-names>DH</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Randomized comparison of two schedules of fluorouracil and leucovorin in the treatment of advanced colorectal cancer</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1994</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>14</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Oncol||12|14||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7677801</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chinery</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Brockman</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Peeler</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name><name><surname>Shyr</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Beauchamp</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Coffey</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antioxidants enhance the cytotoxicity of chemotherapeutic agents in colorectal cancer: a p53-independent i